## Substantive Content

### Regulatory Purpose (§1)
SEBI is conducting survey and creating inventory of AI/ML landscape in Indian financial markets to:
- Gain in-depth understanding of AI/ML adoption in markets
- Ensure preparedness for any AI/ML policies that may arise in the future
- Survey is foundational; reporting is a precondition to policy-making

### Scope Definition (§2–3)

**In scope:** Any applications/software/programs/executables/systems for compliance operations/activities where AI/ML is used for compliance or management purposes. Also includes FinTech and RegTech initiatives by MIIs involving AI/ML.

**AI/ML Technology Categories (Annexure A — six categories):**
1. **NLP, sentiment analysis, text mining** — Voice-to-text, text-to-intelligence, robo chatbots, big data intelligence systems
2. **Neural Networks** — Any system using nodes mimicking natural neural networks (Recurrent NN, Deep Learning NN)
3. **Machine Learning (supervised/unsupervised)** — Decision tree, random forest, K-means, Markov decision process, Gradient boosting
4. **Statistical heuristics / clustering without predefined categories** — Non-procedural algorithmic approaches
5. **Feedback mechanism systems** — Systems that improve parameters through iterative feedback
6. **Knowledge representation systems** — Systems that maintain a knowledge base

### Regulatory Requirements (§4)
- **Mandatory quarterly reporting** (within 15 days of quarter expiry)
- Submission emails: AI_MII_SE@sebi.gov.in / AI_MII_DEP@sebi.gov.in / AI_MII_CC@sebi.gov.in
- Effective from: Quarter ending March 31, 2019

### Reporting Form (Annexure B — 13 data fields)
Entity details, application name, date used from, area of use (order execution/surveillance/compliance/other), tool name, implementation model (internal/provider/joint), SEBI cybersecurity circular alignment, system audit inclusion (Yes/No), application description, safeguards against abnormal behaviour

